Automate financial operations with AI agents.
Install Stripe’s [Model Context Protocol](https://docs.stripe.com/mcp.md) server to automate everyday financial tasks with AI agents. Ask your agent to analyze your data, set up recipients, transfer funds—all while approving sensitive money movement actions. To learn where Treasury is available, see [Availability](https://stripe.com/money-management/availability#explore).
If your MCP client doesn’t support [agent plugins](https://docs.stripe.com/agents/plugin.md) for Stripe, or you prefer to configure the Stripe MCP server and install the skills manually, follow these instructions:

```json
{
"mcpServers": {
"stripe": {
"url": "https://mcp.stripe.com"
}
}
}
```
#### Claude Code
Run the following command to add the Stripe MCP server to Claude Code:
```bash
claude mcp add --transport http stripe https://mcp.stripe.com/
```
After you add the server, start Claude Code and run the `/mcp` command to authenticate Stripe with OAuth.
To authenticate with an [agent API key](https://docs.stripe.com/keys.md#agent-keys) instead of OAuth, add the server to your project’s `.mcp.json` file and reference an environment variable that holds your agent API
